WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What's up?
-What's up, Seth?

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Good to see you guys.
-Hi.

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:03.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi.
-Hi.

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:05.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are bundled up,
Michael Che.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, man.
I'm not used to this weather.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:10.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-I'm from the Island.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:11.711 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:13.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
Manhattan Island.
-Yeah.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:16.416 size:81% position:41%
-You guys are actually
both from the islands.

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:18.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're from
the island of Manhattan.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:18.952 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's right.

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:20.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you're from
the island of Staten.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:21.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.423
[ Laughter ]
-Sounds just as tropical, right?

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Well, they --

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:27.527 size:84% position:42%
Now JetBlue goes direct
to Staten Island, so...

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:29.763 line:92%
-JetBlue has ferry service now.

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:30.964 line:92%
I was gonna come out and wear --

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:32.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was gonna wear
a Hawaiian shirt,

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:33.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he talked me out of it.
-Really?

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And say that I was more
dressing for the job I wanted.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, gotcha.
-Versus this, but then he --

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And the job you wanted
is "Magnum P.I."

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:40.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.610
Why not?
-What job do I want? Panhandler?

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.379 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:49.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
I should be selling batteries
on a D train.

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was so --
You guys had a month off,

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:56.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is unheard of
in my 10 years, which is --

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, we never left.
-You had a month off.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:01.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you enjoy yourselves?
-Uh, yeah.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:03.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:04.130 size:84% position:42% line:92%
You didn't go anywhere.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I had to see
a lot of family.

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
That wasn't fun.
-Really?

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, 'cause, you know,
they just tell me

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:11.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
who else they think is funny.
-Oh, really?

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:12.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know -- I know
what you're talking about.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's not fun to hear.
-Yeah.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:18.745
Do you think that happens
with athletes, like when --

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.680 size:84% position:42%
-"You know who's fast?"
and stuff like that.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Or like Eli Manning at, like,

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:24.150
Thanksgiving dinner, someone's
like, "You know who's great?

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tom Brady."
Like, do you think he --

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
-100%.

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:28.354 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You think 100%.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, based on your own --
don't you think 100%?

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
Based on knowing any family.
-I think they must.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:35.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know who says that to him
is Peyton Manning.

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:36.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Peyton does, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.165 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
As a super burn.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:39.933 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I had a lovely time.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:41.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got to come back
and host this year.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was so fun
to be back with you guys.

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:43.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it was great.
-Got to come back

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:47.173
on the "Update" desk,
which was for me the highlight.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not gonna call it
a low light, but it was not --

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the end, did not turn out
to be a highlight.

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:54.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
You wrote a sketch for me.
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:57.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I should point out,
it was not new business.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:59.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I wrote it
probably about 12 years ago.

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:01.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you resubmitted it
for me, because --

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.456
-And I thought,
"Only you could do this sketch."

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.859
-Well, I -- the actor you
originally wrote it for

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:08.194
is someone that I think
a lot of people mistake me for,

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.663
and so it made sense that you
would try it again with me.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, originally,
it was Taylor Lautner.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:15.068 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:19.205
So I was like, "Who else is in
sort of the 'Twilight' space?"

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. Same fan base.

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:22.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You read
as a classic "Twilight."

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:24.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I was there for that,
so I knew,

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:27.213
"Oh, Jost submitted
a Taylor Lautner sketch for me."

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
So, you're welcome.

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:32.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you want to explain
the premise of Manny Manimal?

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, should we --
-Manny Manimal.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-Manny Manimal.

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:38.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Manny Manimal.
His name was Manny something.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:41.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
He worked
at the radioactive lab

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:43.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
where, like, Spider-Man
had been bitten by a spider.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, the radioactive spider.
-So, this guy,

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:47.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
after he was bitten
by the radioactive spider,

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
he was also bitten
by a radioactive raccoon,

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:52.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
a starfish...
-Yep.

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:54.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-...a pelican...

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:56.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-...a couple snakes...

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:57.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-I think there were like

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:58.778 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
three squirrels?

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:02.215
-And then he died, and a gorilla
had sex with his dead body.

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:03.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
[ Audience groans ]

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Then brought him --
-And then he was revived

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:07.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
by a radioactive parrot.
He was given CPR.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:10.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so, unlike Spider-Man --
-This isn't a real guy.

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, don't worry.
-They're like, "Aww."

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:14.727 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But anyways,
then he is a superhero.

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:19.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was Manny Manimal,
the man of many animals.

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:21.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.436
And you mentioned Emmy-nominated
at the beginning, right?

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:24.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Okay. Great, great.

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:26.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And also,
so his name is Manny Manimal,

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:31.010
the man of many animals, but
also his first name was Manny.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Which was unnecessary.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:34.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Very unnecessary.
-Yeah.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think I found that
late in the writing process.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of the great costumes
of all-time.

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:39.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-There you go.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:41.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:44.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I will say,
great opening title sequence.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Comes out in this.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
